FILE:           T41_drift_inflation.csv
SHA256:         b725304b04fa0724e78e3e85712549d581718f10822c31596ce3fa3e4bc1ff3f
PRODUCER:       code/S43_drift_inflation.R
PRODUCER_SHA256: d193f06a0a5c75ce0b74d4ad9bb324922e1d052ae3d9316c192ccaf159f2167c
INPUTS:
  output/T39_a2_jensen_identity.csv: (per-pair mean_log_eta, var_log_eta)
  output/T40_jensen_control.csv:     (panel-level slopes and reliability)
SEED:           NONE

SPECIFICATION:
  Gates drift-inflation arithmetic from INV-041.
  
  Verifies that the level-route and slope-route derivations of the drift
  inflation factor agree, and that the Control C disattenuation recovers
  the true -0.5 slope.
  
  Level-route: w_level = E[var] / (-2 * E[mean])
  Slope-route: w_slope = 0.5 / |disatt_slope_real|
  
  Under (A2), E[mean] = -E[sigma^2]/2 and E[var] = E[sigma^2].
  With drift: E[var] includes drift, so w > 1.

GATES:
  B1: |w_level - w_slope| / w_level = 0.0053 < 0.05: PASS
  B2: |disatt_slope_ctrlc + 0.5| = 0.0454 < 0.10: PASS
  B3: |predicted - observed| = 0.0014 < 0.01: PASS

KEY VALUES:
  E_mean:               -0.9229
  E_var:                3.5748
  w_level:              1.9367
  w_slope:              1.9265
  disatt_slope_ctrlc:   -0.5454
  predicted_slope:      -0.2582
  observed_slope:       -0.2595

NOTE:
  This closes INV-041 (drift-inflation arithmetic portion).
  The level-route (1.937) and slope-route (1.927) agree to 0.5%.
  Control C recovers -0.5454 from a true -0.5, validating disattenuation.

CREATED: 2026-08-03
